  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>sum-GP-ii-q2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A toy car moves along a straight track and slowly stops. In the first second it moves {@a@} cm. In each next second, it moves a fixed fraction of the distance it moved in the second before. The total distance the car will ever move is {@S@} cm.</p>

<p>(a) Find the common ratio, \(r\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the distance the car moves from second {@j@} onwards, in cm.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Find the distance the car moves before second {@j@}, in cm.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The first term is \( a = {@a@} \) and the sum to infinity is \( S_\infty = {@S@} \).</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common ratio:</strong></p>
<p>Put the values into \( S_\infty = \frac{a}{1 - r} \):</p>
<p>\[ {@S@} = \frac{ {@a@} }{ 1 - r } \]</p>
<p>Multiply both sides by \( 1 - r \):</p>
<p>\[ {@S@}(1 - r) = {@a@} \]</p>
<p>Divide both sides by {@S@}:</p>
<p>\[ 1 - r = \frac{ {@a@} }{ {@S@} } = {@a/S@} \]</p>
<p>\[ r = 1 - {@a/S@} = {@ta1@} \]</p>

<p>(b) <strong>From second {@j@} onwards:</strong></p>
<p>The first term of this new GP is \( T_{ {@j@} } = ar^{ {@j-1@} } = {@a*r^(j-1)@} \). The ratio is still \( {@r@} \):</p>
<p>\[ S_\infty = \frac{ {@a*r^(j-1)@} }{ 1 - {@r@} } = \frac{ {@a*r^(j-1)@} }{ {@1 - r@} } = {@ta2@} \text{ cm} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Before second {@j@}:</strong></p>
<p>Take the distance from second {@j@} onwards away from the total distance:</p>
<p>\[ {@S@} - {@ta2@} = {@ta3@} \text{ cm} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
